WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
In fiscal year 2024, the
federal government paid about

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.570
880 billion dollars in net interest.

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.650
That's more than it spent
on national defense.

4
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.190
Politicians argue about the deficit.

5
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.700
But interest is paid on the debt.

6
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.380
They're not the same thing.

7
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.000
So if the yearly deficit keeps shrinking,

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.350
how can the debt still be growing?

9
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.470
In this mission, you'll
calculate a budget deficit:

10
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.250
government purchases plus
transfers, minus taxes.

11
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.900
Then you'll measure a
country's debt against the size

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.620
of its whole economy.

13
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.260
Your mission: figure out how a
shrinking deficit and a growing

14
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.000
debt can both be true.
